Package: ryzenadj
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: adjust power management settings for AMD Ryzen APUs
 RyzenAdj is a userspace command-line tool for adjusting AMD Ryzen mobile APU
 SMU power management settings. It can set limits such as sustained package
 power and thermal targets on supported Ryzen laptop platforms.
 .
 This package builds the upstream FlyGoat RyzenAdj release used by the HP AMD
 thermal profile tooling, from a pinned and SHA256-verified source tarball.
 Debian and Ubuntu do not package RyzenAdj themselves.
 .
 Kernel lockdown, which Secure Boot normally enables, blocks the low-level SMU
 access this tool needs at runtime.
